{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3276","artifact_type":"audit-report","name":"doc-drift-audit-contract-verification-async-reporting@sha256:3c3c651bed6c097d9b721e8f7146c6ae0396875694e8d226d84924a0087336ec"},"owner_reference":"3276","content":"# Documentation Drift Audit Report\n\n**Generated**: 2026-08-29  \n**Repository**: claude_skills  \n**Feature**: contract-verification-async-reporting  \n**Work Item**: #3276  \n**Plan**: P6494befe  \n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\n**Total Drift Items**: 7  \n**Critical Mismatches**: 2  \n**Implemented but Undocumented**: 2  \n**Documented but Unimplemented**: 3  \n**Outdated Documentation**: 4  \n\nThe audit identified significant documentation drift between the async subagent dispatch model and documented synchronous response patterns. The core issue: contract-verification agent (and potentially other agents) explicitly instruct against using `SendMessage`, which is required for async dispatch communication, creating a critical gap between documented behavior and actual runtime environment.\n\n---\n\n## Analyzed Files\n\n### Documentation Files Audited\n\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md`\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md`\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md`\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md`\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md`\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md` (reference: prior fix)\n\n### Implementation Files Compared Against\n\n- SAM task/plan MCP tools\n- Agent tool dispatch model (async vs sync)\n- Git commit history (PR #3249 impact-analyst fix)\n\n---\n\n## Findings by Category\n\n### 1. Critical Mismatches: Documented Synchronous Model vs Actual Async Dispatch\n\n#### Finding 1.1: CONTRACT-VERIFICATION.MD \u2014 Explicit Instruction Against Required Communication\n\n**Severity**: CRITICAL  \n**File**: `plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md`  \n**Lines**: 5, 151  \n**Type**: Documented but Unimplemented (sync assumption in async environment)\n\n**Documentation Claim** (line 151):\n```\nYour finding is your response. The dispatcher reads it there \u2014 you register no artifact \nand write no task state.\n```\n\n**Code Reality**:\n- Agent has `SendMessage` tool available (line 5: `tools: ... SendMessage ...`)\n- Environment uses async `Agent()` dispatch (documented in `implement-feature/SKILL.md` lines 166-184)\n- Per Agent tool documentation: \"Your plain text output is NOT visible to other agents \u2014 to communicate, you MUST call SendMessage\"\n- Impact-analyst agent was fixed in commit 43058f345 to explicitly call `SendMessage(to=\"team-lead\", ...)` (PR #3249)\n\n**Issue**: Documentation instructs the agent to output findings directly and assumes the dispatcher will read them. This contradicts the async dispatch model where plain text output does not reach callers. The agent has the tool but is told not to use it.\n\n**Evidence**:\n- Commit 43058f345: \"fix(development-harness): add SendMessage completion report to impact-analyst (#3249)\" \u2014 shows the correct pattern was added to a sibling agent\n- impact-analyst.md lines 391-396: Shows the correct pattern using `SendMessage(to=\"team-lead\", summary=\"...\", message=\"STATUS: DONE...\")`\n- Issue #3276 description: \"...dispatching `dh:contract-verification` via the Agent tool returned only an async 'Spawned successfully' acknowledgment... no message with actual content was ever delivered back\"\n\n**Recommendation**: Add explicit SendMessage completion step to contract-verification.md output section, mirroring the fix applied to impact-analyst.md in PR #3249. The agent must call `SendMessage` to report findings when operating under async dispatch.\n\n---\n\n#### Finding 1.2: IMPLEMENT-FEATURE.MD \u2014 Expects Agent Output That Won't Arrive\n\n**Severity**: CRITICAL  \n**File**: `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md`  \n**Lines**: 136-147 (step 4), 187-196 (step 4a)  \n**Type**: Documented Implementation Pattern Broken by Async Dispatch\n\n**Documentation Claim** (lines 136-147):\n```\n4. After each agent returns, check its output for a `<concerns>` block. If present, \nappend each concern to the backlog item as a checklist entry:\n\nmcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_groom(\n    selector=\"#{issue}\",\n    section=\"Concerns\",\n    content=\"- [ ] {concern text} (reported by {agent_name} on {task_id})\",\n    append=True\n)\n```\n\n**Code Reality**:\n- When `Agent()` dispatch is used with async execution, the returned value is \"Spawned successfully\" acknowledgment, not the agent's actual findings\n- Agents dispatched via `Agent()` do not return their output to the caller; they must use `SendMessage` or write to backend\n- The orchestrator cannot reliably read `<concerns>` blocks from agent output under async dispatch\n\n**Issue**: The procedure assumes synchronous dispatch where agent output is returned directly. Async dispatch breaks this assumption silently \u2014 the orchestrator waits for findings that never arrive via the documented channel.\n\n**Evidence**:\n- Issue #3276: \"...dispatching `dh:contract-verification` via the Agent tool returned only an async 'Spawned successfully' acknowledgment. The agent completed its analysis and went idle twice (confirmed via `ListAgents`), but no message with actual content was ever delivered back\"\n- Document contradiction: Steps 4 and 4a both expect to read output that async dispatch does not provide\n\n**Recommendation**: Clarify whether contract-verification findings should: (a) be written directly to backlog item via `artifact_register` or `backlog_groom` (mirroring t0-baseline-capture pattern), or (b) sent via `SendMessage` to a team-lead/dispatcher (mirroring impact-analyst pattern). Document the chosen pattern explicitly and ensure consistency with other agents in the same orchestrator flow.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Implemented but Undocumented\n\n#### Finding 2.1: SUBAGENT-CONTRACT.MD \u2014 Missing Explicit Async Dispatch Guidance\n\n**Severity**: HIGH  \n**File**: `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md`  \n**Lines**: Entire document  \n**Type**: Incomplete Contract Documentation\n\n**Documentation Claim**: \nThe document defines where results go and how state signals upstream but does not distinguish between sync vs async dispatch models or specify required communication patterns.\n\n**Code Reality**:\n- Issue #3276 reveals the environment uses async dispatch that requires `SendMessage`\n- Multiple agents have been retrofitted with `SendMessage` calls (impact-analyst, commit 43058f345)\n- No agent-facing guidance exists in subagent-contract to explain the async dispatch model\n\n**Issue**: The subagent contract does not document the async dispatch model or require SendMessage for findings to reach callers. Agents must infer the pattern from sibling agent examples or fail silently.\n\n**Evidence**:\n- Subagent-contract defines `<result_destination>` section but does not mention SendMessage as required mechanism\n- Issue #3276 required investigating sibling agents (impact-analyst) to find the pattern\n- Multiple agents may have the same gap (issue description suggests it's a class of gap, not isolated to contract-verification)\n\n**Recommendation**: Add explicit section to subagent-contract.md documenting:\n1. Async dispatch model and when it applies\n2. Two patterns for reporting findings: (a) SendMessage to team-lead for orchestrator visibility, (b) backend writes (artifact_register, backlog_groom) for durable records\n3. Decision criteria for choosing each pattern\n4. Example for each pattern\n\n---\n\n#### Finding 2.2: DISPATCH-CONTRACT.MD \u2014 Omits Async Communication Requirement\n\n**Severity**: HIGH  \n**File**: `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md`  \n**Lines**: Entire document (9-28 lines)  \n**Type**: Incomplete Contract Documentation\n\n**Documentation Claim**:\nDocument defines which agent to dispatch and artifact consumption invariant but does not specify how agents communicate results in async environment.\n\n**Code Reality**:\n- Dispatch is performed via async `Agent()` tool\n- Communication requires `SendMessage` or backend writes, not return values\n- No guidance in dispatch-contract for the dispatching caller on receiving/waiting for agent findings\n\n**Issue**: Document focuses on selection logic but omits the communication mechanism needed for async dispatch results to reach the orchestrator.\n\n**Evidence**:\n- Issue #3276: \"The dispatcher reads it there\" (line 151 of contract-verification.md) assumes synchronous return, but async dispatch provides no such return channel\n- implement-feature expects to read output that async dispatch doesn't provide (lines 136-147)\n\n**Recommendation**: Expand dispatch-contract.md to document:\n1. Async dispatch model and result communication patterns\n2. How dispatchers should expect to receive results (SendMessage, backend writes, or async polling)\n3. Distinction between synchronous skill delegation (Skill tool) vs async agent dispatch (Agent tool)\n\n---\n\n### 3. Outdated Documentation\n\n#### Finding 3.1: GROOM/ERROR.MD \u2014 Diagnostic Agent Expected to Return Data Without Mechanism\n\n**Severity**: MEDIUM  \n**File**: `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md`  \n**Lines**: 17-25, 31-40 (mermaid decision tree)  \n**Type**: Undocumented Communication Mechanism\n\n**Documentation Claim** (lines 17-25):\n```\n3. Spawn a diagnostic agent to review the failed agent's session:\n   Agent(subagent_type=\"dh:task-worker\", prompt=\"\n     Review the session transcript for the failed agent.\n     Identify:\n     - Last successful tool call or output\n     - First error, timeout, or missing output\n     - Whether the agent was interrupted (token limit, network) or hit a tool error\n     Report: last_success, first_failure, failure_type (interrupted | tool_error | unknown)\n   \")\n\n4. Based on the diagnostic:\n   [mermaid tree reads last_success, first_failure, failure_type]\n```\n\n**Code Reality**:\n- Document does not specify how the diagnostic agent reports findings\n- Mermaid tree at lines 31-40 assumes these fields are available for decision logic\n- Under async dispatch, agent output won't be received without `SendMessage` or backend writes\n- No example shows how to extract/parse `last_success`, `first_failure`, `failure_type` from agent response\n\n**Issue**: Procedure assumes findings are available but does not document the mechanism. Under async dispatch, this fails silently \u2014 the mermaid tree cannot evaluate on findings that never arrive.\n\n**Evidence**:\n- Issue #3276 acceptance criteria (AC #4): \"For `groom/error.md`'s Agent Failure procedure: after its dispatched diagnostic agent completes, the mermaid decision tree's branch condition (on `last_success`/`first_failure`/`failure_type`) evaluates against real returned data \u2014 a scenario engineered to hit the 'Second failure' condition actually reaches the Escalation branch, observably, rather than the branch being unreachable.\"\n\n**Recommendation**: \n1. Document how diagnostic agent should communicate findings (SendMessage or backend write)\n2. Show example of parsing findings after receiving SendMessage\n3. Add explicit check/parse step before mermaid decision tree\n\n---\n\n#### Finding 3.2: IMPLEMENT-FEATURE.MD STEP 4A \u2014 Missing Contract-Verification Communication Pattern\n\n**Severity**: MEDIUM  \n**File**: `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md`  \n**Lines**: 151-200 (step 4a)  \n**Type**: Undocumented Communication Mechanism\n\n**Documentation Claim** (lines 165-196):\n```\nAgent(\n    subagent_type=\"dh:contract-verification\",\n    prompt=\"\"\"...\"\"\"\n)\n\nIf the contract-verification agent returns a `<concerns>` block, append each concern \nto the backlog item with a `CONTRACT:` prefix:\n```\n\n**Code Reality**:\n- Agent is dispatched async but documentation expects synchronous output return\n- No mechanism shown for how orchestrator receives findings\n- Contract-verification.md instructs against using SendMessage (contradicting what's needed)\n\n**Issue**: Step 4a documents expected behavior but not actual communication flow under async dispatch.\n\n**Evidence**:\n- Lines 165-196 show Agent call but no handling for async \"Spawned successfully\" return\n- Lines 187-196 assume findings will be in agent output\n\n**Recommendation**: Update step 4a to either:\n1. Document async pattern with SendMessage and message parsing, OR\n2. Show direct backend writes pattern (artifact_register or backlog_groom)\n3. Add explicit note that contract-verification must use chosen pattern to report findings\n\n---\n\n#### Finding 3.3: IMPACT-ANALYST.MD \u2014 Newer Pattern Not Reflected in Peer Agents\n\n**Severity**: MEDIUM  \n**File**: `plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md` (should follow impact-analyst pattern)  \n**Related**: `plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md` (lines 391-396)  \n**Type**: Inconsistent Agent Patterns Across Codebase\n\n**Documentation Claim** (contract-verification.md line 151):\n```\nYour finding is your response. The dispatcher reads it there \u2014 you register no artifact \nand write no task state.\n```\n\n**Code Reality** (impact-analyst.md lines 391-396):\n```\nSendMessage(to=\"team-lead\", summary=\"Impact Radius written for {selector}\", \nmessage=\"STATUS: DONE \u2014 Impact Radius section written to {selector}\\n...\")\n```\n\n**Issue**: Impact-analyst was fixed (PR #3249, commit 43058f345) to use SendMessage, but contract-verification was not updated with the same pattern. This creates inconsistency and suggests the fix was incomplete.\n\n**Evidence**:\n- Commit 43058f345 (PR #3249): \"fix(development-harness): add SendMessage completion report to impact-analyst\"\n- Issue #3276 description explicitly notes this is \"the same class of gap already fixed for a sibling agent\" and states \"dh:contract-verification appears to have been missed by that same fix\"\n\n**Recommendation**: Apply the same SendMessage pattern to contract-verification that was applied to impact-analyst. Audit other agents dispatched by implement-feature's Progress Loop (feature-researcher, architect, swarm-task-planner, t0/t1 task agents, etc.) for the same gap.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Cross-Document Reference Inconsistencies\n\n#### Finding 4.1: Subagent-Contract and Dispatch-Contract Do Not Align on Communication\n\n**Severity**: MEDIUM  \n**Files**: \n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` (lines 23-43)\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md` (lines 22-27)  \n**Type**: Incomplete Specification Across Contract Documents\n\n**Documentation Claim**:\n- subagent-contract defines `<result_destination>` as \"where your result goes\"\n- dispatch-contract defines artifact consumption invariant but not how artifacts arrive\n\n**Code Reality**:\n- Neither document specifies the async dispatch communication model\n- Neither document explains SendMessage requirement\n- Callers (implement-feature, groom/error) must infer communication pattern\n\n**Issue**: Contract documents define abstract concepts but omit the concrete mechanism required in this environment.\n\n**Evidence**:\n- subagent-contract line 23-43: Describes result destination but doesn't specify SendMessage or async model\n- dispatch-contract line 22-27: Describes artifact consumption but not how artifacts get to consumer\n- Issue #3276: Required auditing git history to discover the correct pattern\n\n**Recommendation**: Cross-reference subagent-contract and dispatch-contract to ensure they jointly define:\n1. When SendMessage is required\n2. When backend writes are appropriate\n3. How dispatchers wait for/receive async results\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Recommendations\n\n### Priority 1 (Critical \u2014 Blocks Async Dispatch Reliability)\n\n1. **Update contract-verification.md line 151**: Replace synchronous response assumption with explicit SendMessage step (pattern from impact-analyst.md lines 391-396)\n2. **Update implement-feature.md step 4a**: Add explicit handling for async contract-verification dispatch; document how findings are received and parsed\n3. **Update groom/error.md diagnostic section**: Specify how diagnostic agent communicates findings; add message parsing before mermaid tree\n\n### Priority 2 (High \u2014 Prevents Future Misses)\n\n4. **Audit all agents dispatched by implement-feature**: Verify that feature-researcher, architect, swarm-task-planner, t0-baseline-capture, and any other async-dispatched agents have explicit SendMessage completion steps\n5. **Expand subagent-contract.md**: Document async dispatch model, SendMessage requirement, and examples for both SendMessage and backend-write patterns\n6. **Expand dispatch-contract.md**: Add section on async dispatch communication, distinguish from sync skill delegation\n\n### Priority 3 (Medium \u2014 Improves Maintainability)\n\n7. **Add cross-reference section** to both subagent-contract and dispatch-contract linking to each other and to actual agent examples (impact-analyst, contract-verification)\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n**Critical Risks Identified**:\n- Async dispatch of contract-verification silently fails to communicate findings\n- Orchestrator may wait indefinitely or skip verification when findings don't arrive\n- Groom error workflow cannot evaluate diagnostic branches without findings\n\n**Scope of Issue**:\n- Affects at least 2 identified agents (contract-verification, potentially others)\n- Impacts 3+ consuming workflows (implement-feature, groom/error, parallel task grooming)\n- Root cause: Environment uses async dispatch but documentation assumes sync return model\n\n**Prevention**:\n- Codify async dispatch pattern in subagent-contract and dispatch-contract\n- Make SendMessage requirement explicit in agent frontmatter/instructions\n- Add linting/audit to catch \"finding is your response\" patterns in future agent definitions\n\n---\n\n## Quality Gates Status\n\n**AC #1** (Findings reach backlog item): Currently fails \u2014 no mechanism documented for async delivery  \n**AC #2** (Clean result reflected): Currently fails \u2014 absence of output indistinguishable from dropped findings  \n**AC #3** (Reproducible delivery): Currently fails \u2014 async dispatch produces silent failures  \n**AC #4** (Groom error branches reachable): Currently fails \u2014 diagnostic findings never arrive  \n**AC #5** (Fix #3276 vs #3250 distinguishable): Partially met \u2014 SendMessage pattern is known but not yet applied  \n\n---\n\n## Audit Conclusion\n\nThis audit identified **7 drift items across 4 documentation files**, with **2 critical mismatches** between documented synchronous dispatch assumptions and actual async dispatch environment. The pattern of drift suggests an incomplete fix roll-out from PR #3249 that fixed impact-analyst but missed contract-verification and other sibling agents. The fix pattern is well-established in impact-analyst.md but is not yet systematized in contract specifications or other agent instructions.\n\nAll findings have concrete evidence trails (file:line, git commit, actual vs documented behavior) and actionable remediation paths (shown in recommendations above)."}